    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "BUILD",
      "role_note": "Software Walkthrough scene, section BUILD",
      "narration_text": "Here is how I will build it. First, fetch. Early Bird will read the public job boards of Greenhouse, Lever and Ashby. These are public data, with no login. In my Commure test, one snapshot had eighty one postings. Second, compare. Early Bird will check each posting against a file of what I have already seen. In my test, twelve of the eighty one were new. Third, judge. Plain rules will come first. Then Claude Sonnet five point five will read each posting. It will never skip a job for a skill gap. It will only flag a hard blocker, and quote the line. My probe showed why. A rule alone matched a sales job called Account Executive, A I Sales. Fourth, match. Each posting will be matched to my real GitHub projects. Fifth, order. Referral first, then freshness, then match. For referrals, Early Bird will look up my own LinkedIn connections file, and that file will stay on my laptop. Sixth, a report, one file for each run.",
